\ Companion module for task_load_lock_contention.1z. Its top level parks the
\ loading task mid-load with a bare sleep, which a load run from a task may do.
\ The two markers bracket the suspension window.
\
\ It lives under fixtures/ because it cannot run as a program of its own: with
\ no scheduler, the sleep raises.

use "time" ;

"SLOW-MOD-START" print-line

5 milliseconds sleep

"SLOW-MOD-END" print-line

slow-word: ( -- s ) [ "slow" ] ;
